# Variable names and descriptions only. OpenShift Secret values are supplied at deployment time.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL: Same-origin API base path.
# DATABASE_URL: Async PostgreSQL DSN for the API or seed writer, supplied from an OpenShift Secret.
# OGX_BASE_URL: Namespace-local OGX Responses API endpoint used by the API.
# PREDICTION_MCP_URL: Namespace-local prediction MCP endpoint.
# DATA_FETCH_MCP_URL: Namespace-local data-fetch MCP endpoint.
# SCORING_BATCH_SIZE: Maximum identifiers sent to one MCP prediction call.
# OGX_DATABASE_URL: PostgreSQL metadata/session connection supplied from an OpenShift Secret.
# OGX_MODEL_ID: Explicit configured Llama model identifier.
# LLM_MODEL_ID: On-cluster model ID used by vLLM and OGX.
# REMOTE_LLM_BASE_URL: Optional deployment-time remote endpoint.
# REMOTE_LLM_API_KEY: Optional remote endpoint credential from an OpenShift Secret.
# CHURN_MODEL_URI: External S3-compatible churn artifact prefix.
# CHURN_STORAGE_SECRET: Existing namespace-scoped S3 connection Secret name for churn serving.
# FRAUD_MODEL_URI: External S3-compatible fraud artifact prefix.
# FRAUD_STORAGE_SECRET: Existing namespace-scoped S3 connection Secret name for fraud serving.
# QOE_MODEL_URI: External S3-compatible QoE artifact prefix.
# QOE_STORAGE_SECRET: Existing namespace-scoped S3 connection Secret name for QoE serving.
# DATA_FETCH_MCP_URL: Internal data-fetch MCP endpoint used by prediction tools.
# CHURN_MODEL_URL: Namespace-local KServe V2 churn endpoint.
# FRAUD_MODEL_URL: Namespace-local KServe V2 fraud endpoint.
# QOE_MODEL_URL: Namespace-local KServe V2 QoE endpoint.
# MODEL_FEATURE_MANIFEST_DIR: Read-only location for feature manifests and preprocessing sidecar references.
# DATABASE_READONLY_URL: Read-only async PostgreSQL DSN supplied from an OpenShift Secret.
# MCP_HOST: Internal service bind host.
# MCP_PORT: Internal service port.
# MAX_FETCH_ROWS: Maximum rows returned by one data-fetch tool call.
# GENERATOR_SEED: Seed for repeatable synthetic joins and regional assignment.
# REGIONAL_QOE_CHURN_COUPLING: Tunable strength of the synthetic regional relationship.
# INGEST_BATCH_SIZE: Bounded database insert/upsert batch size.
